CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^EXIT=(0|10)$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^PARSING ERROR$
A std::function whose function-type argument names its parameter denotes
the same specialization as the unnamed spelling and must elaborate its
operator bool, so the contextual conversion to bool in ready compiles
without a CONVERSION ERROR. This is a front-end type-checking regression
test; std::function's runtime model is not the subject here.
